  "claim_command_output": "2538\n# NEW S64a time-warped template pulse-shape timing under pedestal drift and pile-up\n\nAcademic-grade study: quantify how pedestal drift, sub-sample timing phase, and early pile-up distort pulse shape and timing. Compare a traditional time-warped matched-template/constant-fraction discriminator baseline against ridge regression on engineered waveform moments, gradient-boosted trees on shape/timing features, an MLP on normalized windows, a 1D-CNN on raw waveforms, and a compact waveform transformer where statistics allow. Report bootstrap CIs for timing bias/resolution, shape residuals, pile-up strata, pedestal bins, energy slices, and PID-conditioned residuals; include ablations for saturation masks and pre-trigger pedestal estimates.\n",
